      "math_academy_id": "q-129446",
      "knowledge_point_id": "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=x\\sqrt{y}-y\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(1,4,-2).$",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{y}-y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\sqrt{y}-y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}}-\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,4) & =\\sqrt{4}-\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{1}}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,4) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}-\\sqrt{1}=-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-(-2) & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,4)+(y-4)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,4) \\\\ z+2 & =0(x-1)-\\frac{3}{4}(y-4) \\\\ z+2 & =-\\frac{3}{4}y+3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}y+z-1 & =0 \\\\ 3y+4z-4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
